{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-deu-10-1","title":"Deuteronomy 10:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God's mercy in restoring the two tables; 6 in continuing the priesthood; 8 in separating the tribe of Levi; 10 in hearkening unto Moses' suit for his people. 12 An exhortation to obedience.</p>\n<p>Hew. 4; Ex 34:1,2,4 make thee. 3; Ex 25:10-15; Heb 9:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-2","title":"Deuteronomy 10:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>thou shalt. 5; Ex 25:16-22; 40:20; 1Ki 8:9; Heb 9:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-3","title":"Deuteronomy 10:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>I made. Ex 25:5,10; 37:1-9 hewed. 1; Ex 34:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-4","title":"Deuteronomy 10:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>he wrote. 9:10; Ex 34:28 the ten. 4:13 commandments. Heb. words. which. 5:4-21; Ex 20:1-17 out of the. 4:11-15; 5:22-26; Ex 19:18; Heb 12:18,19 in the day. 9:10; 18:16; Ex 19:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-5","title":"Deuteronomy 10:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>I turned. 9:15; Ex 32:15; 34:29 put the. 2; Ex 25:16; 40:20 there they. Jos 4:9; 1Ki 8:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-6","title":"Deuteronomy 10:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>took. Nu 10:6,12,13; 33:1,2 Mosera. Nu 33:30-33 Moseroth, Hor-ha-gid-gad, Jotbathah. there Aaron. Nu 20:23-28; 33:38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-8","title":"Deuteronomy 10:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>time the Lord. Ex 29:1-37; Le 8:9; Nu 1:47-53; 3:1-4:49; 8:1-26; 16:9,10; 18:1-32 Joh 15:16; Ac 13:2; Ro 1:1; 2Co 6:17; Ga 1:15 bear. Nu 3:31; 4:15; 1Ki 8:3,4,6; 1Ch 15:12-15,26; 23:26; 2Ch 5:4,5 to stand. 18:5; 2Ch 29:11; Ps 134:2; 135:2; Jer 15:19; Eze 44:11,15; Ro 12:7 to bless. 21:5; Le 9:22; Nu 6:23-26; 2Ch 30:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-9","title":"Deuteronomy 10:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>18:1,2; Nu 18:20-24; 26:62; Jos 14:3; Eze 44:28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-10","title":"Deuteronomy 10:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>I stayed. 9:18,25; Ex 24:18; 34:28 first time. or, former days. the Lord hearkened. 3:23-27; 9:19; Ex 32:14,33,34; 33:17; Mt 27:42</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-11","title":"Deuteronomy 10:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Arise. Ex 32:34; 33:1 take thy. Heb. go in.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-12","title":"Deuteronomy 10:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>what doth. Jer 7:22,23; Mic 6:8; Mt 11:29,30; 1Jo 5:3 fear. 6:13; Ps 34:9; 128:1; Jer 32:39,40; Ac 9:31; 1Pe 1:17 to walk. 5:33; Jos 22:5; Ps 81:13; Eze 11:20; Tit 2:11,12; 1Pe 1:15,16 love. 6:5; 11:13; 30:16,20; Ps 18:1; 145:20; Mt 22:37; Mr 12:29-33 Lu 10:27; 11:42; Ro 8:28; 1Jo 2:15; 4:19,20; 5:2,5 to serve. Job 36:11; Zep 3:9; Ro 1:9; Heb 12:28 God with all. 4:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-13","title":"Deuteronomy 10:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>for thy. 6:24; Pr 9:12; Jer 32:39; Jas 1:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-14","title":"Deuteronomy 10:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>the heaven. 1Ki 8:27; 2Ch 6:18; Ne 9:6; Ps 115:16; 148:4; Isa 66:1 the earth. Ge 14:19; Ex 9:29; 19:5; Ps 24:1; 50:12; Jer 27:5,6; 1Co 10:26,28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-15","title":"Deuteronomy 10:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>4:37; 7:7,8; Nu 14:8; Ro 9:13-23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-16","title":"Deuteronomy 10:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Circumcise. 30:6; Le 26:41; Jer 4:4,14; Ro 2:28,29; Col 2:11 stiff-necked. 9:6,13; 31:27; Jas 4:6,7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-17","title":"Deuteronomy 10:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>God of gods. Jos 22:22; 1Ch 16:25,26; Ps 136:2; Da 2:47; 11:36 Lord of lords. Ps 136:3; Re 17:14; 19:16 a great. 7:21; Ne 1:5; 4:14; 9:32; Job 37:22,23; Ps 99:3; Jer 20:11 regardeth. 2Ch 19:7; Job 34:19; Mr 12:14; Ac 10:34; Ro 2:11; Ga 2:6; Eph 6:9 Col 3:25; 1Pe 1:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-18","title":"Deuteronomy 10:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>doth. Ps 68:5; 103:6; 146:9; Isa 1:17; Jer 49:11; Ho 14:3 loveth. Ps 145:9; Mt 5:45; Ac 14:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-19","title":"Deuteronomy 10:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>Ex 22:21; Le 19:33,34; Lu 6:35; 10:28-37; 17:18; Ga 6:10 Jas 2:15,16; 1Jo 3:17,18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-20","title":"Deuteronomy 10:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>fear. 6:13; 13:4; Mt 4:10; Lu 4:8 cleave. 4:4; 11:22; 13:4; Jos 23:8; Ac 11:23; Ro 12:9 swear. 6:13; Ps 63:11; Isa 45:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-21","title":"Deuteronomy 10:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>thy praise. Ex 15:2; Ps 22:3; Isa 12:2-6; 60:19; Jer 17:14; Lu 2:32; Re 21:23 that hath. 4:32-35; 1Sa 12:24; 2Sa 7:23; Ps 106:21,22; Isa 64:3; Jer 32:20,21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-deu-10-22","title":"Deuteronomy 10:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"DEU","chapterStart":10,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":10,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>with threescore.And now, from so small a beginning, they are multiplied to more than 600,000 men, besides women and children; and this, indeed, in the space of 40 years; for the 603,000 which came out of Egypt were at this time all dead, except Moses, Joshua, and Caleb. How easy can God increase and multiply, as well as diminish and bring low! In all things, by his omnipotence, he can do whatsoever he will; and he will do whatsoever is right.</p>\n<p>Ge 46:27; Ex 1:5; Ac 7:14 as the stars. 1:10; 28:62; Ge 15:5; Nu 26:51,62; Ne 9:23; Heb 11:12</p>"}]}